,"bih-tee-ROO"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Kazakh often drops the pronoun, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. There is no he / she difference: \"ол\" means both."],"rows":[["I","мен","men"],["you (informal)","сен","sen"],["he / she / it","ол","ol"],["we","біз","biz"],["you (formal or plural)","сіз","seez"],["they","олар","o-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am a student","мен студентпін","men stoo-dent-PIN"],["you are tall","сен ұзынсың","sen oo-zuhn-SUHNG"],["she is my older sister","ол менің апам","ol meh-NING ah-PAM"],["we are friends","біз доспыз","biz dos-PUHZ"],["they are teachers","олар мұғалімдер","o-LAR moo-gha-lim-DER"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -лар, -лер, -дар, -дер, -тар or -тер, by vowel harmony and the last sound. After a number, the noun stays singular: екі кітап (two book)."],"rows":[["кітап (book)","кітаптар","kee-tap-TAR"],["үй (house)","үйлер","ewy-LER"],["бала (child)","балалар","bah-lah-LAR"],["after a number: singular","екі кітап","yeh-KEE kee-TAP"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","бір үй, үйлер","bihr EWY ewy-LER"],["one book, books","бір кітап, кітаптар","bihr kee-TAP kee-tap-TAR"],["one cat, cats","бір мысық, мысықтар","bihr muh-SUHK muh-suhk-TAR"],["two books","екі кітап","yeh-KEE kee-TAP"],["the children","балалар","bah-lah-LAR"]]},{"id":"to-be","title":"To be: -мын, -сың, -мыз","text":["There is no separate verb \"to be\". Add an ending to the noun or adjective. The ending changes by vowel harmony: -мын / -мін / -бын / -бін / -пын / -пін."],"rows":[["I am","-мын / -мін","muhn"],["you are","-сың / -сің","suhng"],["he / she is","(no ending)","-"],["we are","-мыз / -міз","muhz"],["you are (formal)","-сыз / -сіз","suhz"],["they are","-лар / -лер","lar"]],"ex":[["I am a student","мен студентпін","men stoo-dent-PIN"],["you are tired","сен шаршағансың","sen shar-shah-ghan-SUHNG"],["he is a doctor","ол дәрігер","ol dah-ree-GER"],["we are happy","біз бақыттымыз","biz bah-kuht-tuh-MUHZ"],["they are at home","олар үйде","o-LAR ewy-DEH"]]},{"id":"bar-and-joq-have-there-is","title":"Bar and joq: have, there is","text":["Kazakh says \"at me there is\" (бар) or \"at me there is not\" (жоқ). The ending -да / -де means \"at\" or \"in\"."],"rows":[["there is","бар","bar"],["there is not","жоқ","zhok"],["I have","менде ... бар","men-DEH bar"],["I do not have","менде ... жоқ","men-DEH zhok"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","менде аға бар","men-DEH ah-GHAH bar"],["I have a car","менде көлік бар","men-DEH kur-LIK bar"],["I do not have time","менде уақыт жоқ","men-DEH oo-ah-KUHT zhok"],["there is a problem","мәселе бар","mah-seh-LEH bar"],["there is no water","су жоқ","soo zhok"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Verb stem + а / е / й + person ending. Келу (to come): кел-е-мін."],"rows":[["I come","келемін","keh-leh-MIN"],["you come","келесің","keh-leh-SING"],["he / she comes","келеді","keh-leh-DEE"],["we come","келеміз","keh-leh-MIZ"],["you come (formal)","келесіз","keh-leh-SEEZ"],["they come","келеді","keh-leh-DEE"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","мен нан жеп жатырмын","men nan zhep zhah-tuhr-MUHN"],["you are reading a book","сен кітап оқып жатырсың","sen kee-TAP o-KUHP zhah-tuhr-SUHNG"],["she works in a bank","ол банкте жұмыс істейді","ol bank-TEH zhoo-MUHS is-tay-DEE"],["we drink tea","біз шай ішеміз","biz shai ee-sheh-MIZ"],["they are sleeping","олар ұйықтап жатыр","o-LAR oy-uhk-TAP zhah-TUHR"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb goes last. Order: who, where or when, what, verb. Kazakh has no articles: \"кітап\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","мен кітап оқимын","men kee-TAP o-kuh-MUHN"],["she drinks tea","ол шай ішеді","ol shai ee-sheh-DEE"],["we go to school","біз мектепке барамыз","biz mek-tep-KEH bah-rah-MUHZ"]],"ex":[["I read a book","мен кітап оқимын","men kee-TAP o-kuh-MUHN"],["he drinks tea","ол шай ішеді","ol shai ee-sheh-DEE"],["we go to school","біз мектепке барамыз","biz mek-tep-KEH bah-rah-MUHZ"],["they eat bread","олар нан жейді","o-LAR nan zhay-DEE"],["the teacher writes","мұғалім жазады","moo-gha-LIM zhah-zah-DUH"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put -ма / -ме / -ба / -бе / -па / -пе after the verb stem: барамын (I go), бармаймын (I do not go). For nouns use \"емес\" (is not). \"Жоқ\" means \"there is not\". Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["I go","барамын","bah-rah-MUHN"],["I do not go","бармаймын","bar-mai-MUHN"],["is","(no ending)","-"],["is not","емес","yeh-MES"]],"ex":[["I want","мен қалаймын","men kah-lai-MUHN"],["I do not want","мен қаламаймын","men kah-lah-mai-MUHN"],["I speak English","мен ағылшынша сөйлеймін","men ah-ghuhl-shuhn-SHAH sur-lay-MIN"],["I do not speak English","мен ағылшынша сөйлемеймін","men ah-ghuhl-shuhn-SHAH sur-leh-meh-MIN"],["I like it","маған ұнайды","mah-GHAN oo-nai-DUH"],["I do not like it","маған ұнамайды","mah-GHAN oo-nah-mai-DUH"],["she is here","ол осында","ol o-suhn-DAH"],["she is not here","ол осында емес","ol o-suhn-DAH yeh-MES"],["I have a car","менде көлік бар","men-DEH kur-LIK bar"],["I do not have a car","менде көлік жоқ","men-DEH kur-LIK zhok"],["I understand","түсінемін","tew-see-neh-MIN"],["I do not understand","түсінбеймін","tew-sin-beh-MIN"],["we are tired","біз шаршағанбыз","biz shar-shah-ghan-BUHZ"],["we are not tired","біз шаршаған жоқпыз","biz shar-shah-GHAN zhok-PUHZ"],["he works on Sundays","ол жексенбіде жұмыс істейді","ol zhek-sen-bee-DEH zhoo-MUHS is-tay-DEE"],["he does not work on Sundays","ол жексенбіде жұмыс істемейді","ol zhek-sen-bee-DEH zhoo-MUHS is-teh-may-DEE"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add the little word ба / бе / па / пе / ма / ме after the word you are asking about. It is the same for every question."],"rows":[["you are a student","сіз студентсіз","seez stoo-dent-SEEZ"],["are you a student?","сіз студентсіз бе?","seez stoo-dent-SEEZ beh"],["he is here","ол осында","ol o-suhn-DAH"],["is he here?","ол осында ма?","ol o-suhn-DAH mah"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","бұл сіздің кітабыңыз ба?","bool seez-DING kee-tah-buhng-UHZ bah"],["are they here?","олар осында ма?","o-LAR o-suhn-DAH mah"],["do you like tea?","сіз шайды ұнатасыз ба?","seez shai-DUH oo-nah-tah-SUHZ bah"],["is it cold?","суық па?","soo-UHK pah"],["do you speak English?","сіз ағылшынша сөйлейсіз бе?","seez ah-ghuhl-shuhn-SHAH sur-lay-SEEZ beh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand where the answer would stand."],"rows":[["what","не","neh"],["who","кім","kim"],["where","қайда","kai-DAH"],["when","қашан","kah-SHAN"],["why","неге","neh-GEH"],["how","қалай","kah-LAI"],["how much","қанша","kan-SHAH"],["which","қай","kai"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","атыңыз кім?","ah-tuh-NUHZ KIM"],["who is he?","ол кім?","ol KIM"],["where do you live?","сіз қайда тұрасыз?","seez kai-DAH too-rah-SUHZ"],["when is the lesson?","сабақ қашан?","sah-BAK kah-SHAN"],["why are you late?","неге кешіктіңіз?","neh-GEH keh-shik-tee-NIZ"],["how are you?","қалайсыз?","kah-lai-SUHZ"],["how much is it?","қанша тұрады?","kan-SHAH too-rah-DUH"],["which book?","қай кітап?","kai kee-TAP"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Endings go on the noun: -ым / -ім (my), -ың / -ің (your), -ы / -і (his / her). To say you like something, use \"маған ұнайды\" (to me it is pleasing)."],"rows":[["my book","кітабым","kee-tah-BUHM"],["your book","кітабың","kee-tah-BUHNG"],["his / her book","кітабы","kee-tah-BUH"],["our book","кітабымыз","kee-tah-buh-MUHZ"],["your book (formal)","кітабыңыз","kee-tah-buhng-UHZ"]],"ex":[["my phone","телефоным","teh-leh-fo-NUHM"],["your house (formal)","үйіңіз","ewy-ing-IZ"],["his sister","оның қарындасы","o-NUHNG kah-ruhn-dah-SUH"],["I like music","маған музыка ұнайды","mah-GHAN moo-zuh-KAH oo-nai-DUH"],["I love football","мен футболды жақсы көремін","men foot-bol-DUH zhak-SUH kur-reh-MIN"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["сен (informal): friends, family, children. сіз (formal): strangers, older people, work. Verb endings change: -сың (informal), -сыз (formal)."],"rows":[["how are you?","қалайсың? / қалайсыз?","kah-lai-SUHNG / kah-lai-SUHZ"],["you speak","сөйлейсің / сөйлейсіз","sur-lay-SING / sur-lay-SEEZ"],["your name","атың / атыңыз","ah-TUHNG / ah-tuh-NUHZ"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","қалайсың?","kah-lai-SUHNG"],["how are you? (formal)","қалайсыз?","kah-lai-SUHZ"],["where are you going? (informal)","қайда барасың?","kai-DAH bah-rah-SUHNG"],["where are you going? (formal)","қайда барасыз?","kai-DAH bah-rah-SUHZ"],["please sit down (formal)","отырыңыз, өтінемін","o-tuh-ruhng-UHZ uh-tee-neh-MIN"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: -ды / -ді / -ты / -ті + person ending (бардым = I went). Future uses the present form with a time word: ертең барамын (tomorrow I go)."],"rows":[["I went","бардым","bar-DUHM"],["you went","бардың","bar-DUHNG"],["he went","барды","bar-DUH"],["we went","бардық","bar-DUHK"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","кеше шаршадым","keh-SHEH shar-shah-DUHM"],["I will study tomorrow","ертең оқимын","er-TENG o-kuh-MUHN"],["we went to the park","біз саябаққа бардық","biz sah-yah-bak-KAH bar-DUHK"],["I saw him","мен оны көрдім","men o-NUH kur-DIM"],["she wrote a letter","ол хат жазды","ol khat zhaz-DUH"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the bare verb stem. Formal: add -ыңыз / -іңіз. To forbid, add -ма / -ме after the stem."],"rows":[["come (informal)","кел","kel"],["come (formal)","келіңіз","keh-lin-IZ"],["do not come","келме","kel-MEH"],["sit down","отыр","o-TUHR"]],"ex":[["come here","мұнда кел","moon-DAH KEL"],["do not come here","мұнда келме","moon-DAH kel-MEH"],["sit down","отыр","o-TUHR"],["do not sit down","отырма","o-tuhr-MAH"],["be quiet","үнсіз бол","ewn-SEEZ bol"],["do not be late","кешікпе","keh-shik-PEH"],["open the door","есікті аш","eh-sik-TEE ASH"],["close the window","терезені жап","teh-reh-zeh-NEE ZHAP"],["listen to me","мені тыңда","meh-NEE tuhng-DAH"],["do not worry","уайымдама","oo-ai-uhm-dah-MAH"],["speak slowly","баяу сөйле","bah-YAO sur-LEH"],["wait a moment","бір сәт күт","bihr SAHT KEWT"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: verb + а алу (жүзе аламын, I can swim). Must: \"керек\" (needed). Want: -ғым келеді (жегім келеді, I want to eat)."],"rows":[["I can swim","жүзе аламын","zhew-ZEH ah-lah-MUHN"],["I cannot swim","жүзе алмаймын","zhew-ZEH al-mai-MUHN"],["I must go","баруым керек","bah-roo-UHM keh-REK"],["I want to go","барғым келеді","bar-ghuhm keh-leh-DEE"]],"ex":[["I can swim","мен жүзе аламын","men zhew-ZEH ah-lah-MUHN"],["I cannot swim","мен жүзе алмаймын","men zhew-ZEH al-mai-MUHN"],["can you help me?","маған көмектесе аласыз ба?","mah-GHAN kur-mek-teh-SEH ah-lah-SUHZ bah"],["we must go","біз баруымыз керек","biz bah-roo-uh-MUHZ keh-REK"],["we must not go","біз бармауымыз керек","biz bar-mah-oo-uh-MUHZ keh-REK"],["I want to eat","жегім келеді","zheh-GIM keh-leh-DEE"],["I do not want to eat","жегім келмейді","zheh-GIM kel-may-DEE"],["you can come","келуге болады","keh-loo-GEH bo-lah-DUH"],["you cannot come","келуге болмайды","keh-loo-GEH bol-mai-DUH"],["she wants to study","оның оқығысы келеді","o-NUHNG o-kuh-ghuh-suh keh-leh-DEE"],["I must work today","бүгін жұмыс істеуім керек","bew-GIN zhoo-MUHS is-teh-oo-IM keh-REK"],["you must not run","жүгіруге болмайды","zhew-gee-roo-GEH bol-mai-DUH"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Kazakh uses endings, not words in front: -да / -де (in, on, at), -ға / -ге (to), -дан / -ден (from), -ның / -нің (of)."],"rows":[["in / on / at","-да / -де","dah / deh"],["to","-ға / -ге","ghah / geh"],["from","-дан / -ден","dan / den"],["of","-ның / -нің","nuhng / ning"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","кітап үстелде","kee-TAP ews-tel-DEH"],["the cat is under the table","мысық үстелдің астында","muh-SUHK ews-tel-DING as-tuhn-DAH"],["I am at school","мен мектептемін","men mek-tep-teh-MIN"],["I am at home","мен үйдемін","men ewy-deh-MIN"],["the shop is next to the bank","дүкен банктің жанында","dew-KEN bank-TING zhah-nuhn-DAH"],["the park is near the station","саябақ вокзалға жақын","sah-yah-BAK vok-zal-GHAH zhah-KUHN"],["we meet in the morning","біз таңертең кездесеміз","biz tang-er-TENG kez-deh-seh-MIZ"],["the lesson is at nine","сабақ сағат тоғызда","sah-BAK sah-GHAT toh-ghuhz-DAH"],["the key is in the bag","кілт сөмкеде","kilt surm-keh-DEH"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add -рақ / -рек to the adjective for \"more\": үлкен, үлкенірек. For \"the most\" put \"ең\" before it: ең үлкен. \"Than\" is -дан / -ден."],"rows":[["big, bigger, the biggest","үлкен, үлкенірек, ең үлкен","ewl-KEN ewl-keh-nee-REK en ewl-KEN"],["small, smaller, the smallest","кіші, кішірек, ең кіші","kee-SHEE kee-shee-REK en kee-SHEE"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","үлкен, үлкенірек, ең үлкен","ewl-KEN ewl-keh-nee-REK en ewl-KEN"],["small, smaller, the smallest","кіші, кішірек, ең кіші","kee-SHEE kee-shee-REK en kee-SHEE"],["this is better than that","бұл анадан жақсы","bool ah-nah-DAN zhak-SUH"],["this is worse than that","бұл анадан жаман","bool ah-nah-DAN zhah-MAN"],["she is taller than me","ол менен ұзынырақ","ol meh-NEN oo-zuh-nuh-RAK"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Ташкент Самарқаннан үлкенірек","tash-KENT sah-mar-kan-NAN ewl-keh-nee-REK"],["it is the cheapest","бұл ең арзан","bool en ar-ZAN"],["the same as","сияқты","see-yak-TUH"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","ол мұғалім","ol moo-gha-LIM"],["you (plural) are students","сіздер студенттерсіздер","seez-DER stoo-dent-ter-seez-DER"],["I am happy","мен бақыттымын","men bah-kuht-tuh-MUHN"],["she is at school","ол мектепте","ol mek-tep-TEH"],["you are my friend","сен менің досымсың","sen meh-NING do-suhm-SUHNG"],["it is cold","суық","soo-UHK"],["I study English","мен ағылшын тілін үйреніп жүрмін","men ah-ghuhl-SHUHN tee-LIN ewy-reh-NIP zhewr-MIN"],["he teaches maths","ол математика оқытады","ol mah-teh-MAH-tee-kah o-kuh-tah-DUH"],["they work every day","олар күн сайын жұмыс істейді","o-LAR kewn sai-UHN zhoo-MUHS is-tay-DEE"],["is this your book?","бұл сіздің кітабыңыз ба?","bool seez-DING kee-tah-buhng-UHZ bah"],["are they here?","олар осында ма?","o-LAR o-suhn-DAH mah"],["do you like tea?","сіз шайды ұнатасыз ба?","seez shai-DUH oo-nah-tah-SUHZ bah"],["what time is it?","сағат неше?","sah-GHAT neh-SHEH"],["whose book is this?","бұл кімнің кітабы?","bool kim-NING kee-tah-BUH"],["how old are you?","сіз неше жастасыз?","seez neh-SHEH zhas-tah-SUHZ"],["how do you say it?","мұны қалай айтасыз?","moo-NUH kah-LAI ai-tah-SUHZ"],["your book (formal)","кітабыңыз","kee-tah-buhng-UHZ"],["their house","олардың үйі","o-lar-DUHNG ewy-EE"],["my phone","телефоным","teh-leh-fo-NUHM"],["excuse me, sir","кешіріңіз, мырза","keh-shee-ree-NIZ muhr-ZAH"],["please sit down (formal)","отырыңыз, өтінемін","o-tuh-ruhng-UHZ uh-tee-neh-MIN"],["come here (informal)","мұнда кел","moon-DAH KEL"],["yesterday I was tired","кеше шаршадым","keh-SHEH shar-shah-DUHM"],["I will study tomorrow","ертең оқимын","er-TENG o-kuh-MUHN"],["we went to the park","біз саябаққа бардық","biz sah-yah-bak-KAH bar-DUHK"]]}],"name":"Kazakh","id":"kk","flag":"kz","note":""}